{% comment %}
  Hair-loss fit quiz. Three questions, one result screen that tells the visitor how well Elaren fits
  the KIND of hair loss they have. It never quotes a probability: the result is a band with a reason.

  Blocks:
    question  - one question (order in the sidebar = order asked)
    option    - an answer; "Belongs to question" says which question it appears under and "Points to"
                the hair-loss type it suggests (pattern / shedding / traction / medical / none)
    result    - the screen shown for one band (pattern, shedding, traction, medical)

  How the band is decided (assets/main.js, initFitQuiz):
    1. any answer pointing to "medical" wins - those visitors are told to see a doctor, not to buy;
    2. otherwise any answer pointing to "traction" wins;
    3. otherwise whichever of "pattern" / "shedding" collected more answers, pattern on a tie.
  Every result can hand the visitor to the buy box with a bundle tier pre-selected.
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign questions = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'question'
  assign options = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'option'
  assign results = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'result'
  assign cta_target = section.settings.cta_link | default: '#product-section' | remove: '#'
  comment
    Placeholders are swapped inside this liquid tag: a literal "{" in an output tag trips Shopify's parser.
  endcomment
  assign current_placeholder = '{current}'
  assign total_placeholder = '{total}'
  assign step_text = section.settings.step_label | replace: current_placeholder, '1' | replace: total_placeholder, questions.size
-%}
<section class="shopify-section section" id="shopify-section-{{ section.id }}-fit-quiz">
<div class="s-fit-quiz custom-section{% if section.settings.background %} s-fit-quiz--background{% endif %}" data-fit-quiz data-section-id="{{ section.id }}">
  <div class="s-fit-quiz__container">
    <header class="s-fit-quiz__head">
      {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}<p class="s-fit-quiz__eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</p>{%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.title != blank -%}<h2 class="s-fit-quiz__title section-title"><p>{{ section.settings.title }}</p></h2>{%- endif -%}
      {%- if section.settings.text != blank -%}<div class="s-fit-quiz__intro">{{ section.settings.text }}</div>{%- endif -%}
    </header>

    <div class="s-fit-quiz__card" data-quiz-card>
      {%- if questions.size > 0 -%}
      <div class="s-fit-quiz__progress" data-quiz-progress>
        <span class="s-fit-quiz__step" data-quiz-step>{{ step_text }}</span>
        <span class="s-fit-quiz__dots" aria-hidden="true">
          {%- for question in questions -%}<span class="s-fit-quiz__dot{% if forloop.first %} is-active{% endif %}"></span>{%- endfor -%}
        </span>
      </div>

      {%- for question in questions -%}
        <fieldset class="s-fit-quiz__question{% unless forloop.first %} is-hidden{% endunless %}" data-quiz-question="{{ forloop.index }}" {{ question.shopify_attributes }}>
          <legend class="s-fit-quiz__question-title">{{ question.settings.text }}</legend>
          {%- if question.settings.hint != blank -%}<p class="s-fit-quiz__question-hint">{{ question.settings.hint }}</p>{%- endif -%}
          <div class="s-fit-quiz__options">
            {%- for option in options -%}
              {%- if option.settings.question == forloop.parentloop.index -%}
              <button class="s-fit-quiz__option" type="button" data-quiz-option data-band="{{ option.settings.band }}" {{ option.shopify_attributes }}>
                <span class="s-fit-quiz__option-check" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <span class="s-fit-quiz__option-label">{{ option.settings.label }}</span>
                {%- if option.settings.note != blank -%}<span class="s-fit-quiz__option-note" data-quiz-note hidden>{{ option.settings.note }}</span>{%- endif -%}
              </button>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        </fieldset>
      {%- endfor -%}

      <div class="s-fit-quiz__nav">
        <button class="s-fit-quiz__back" type="button" data-quiz-back hidden>{{ section.settings.back_label }}</button>
      </div>
      {%- elsif request.design_mode -%}
      <p class="s-fit-quiz__empty">Add "Question" and "Answer" blocks to build the quiz.</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- for result in results -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign tier = result.settings.bundle_tier | default: 0
          assign cta_label = result.settings.cta_label
          if cta_label == blank
            assign cta_label = section.settings.cta_label
          endif
        -%}
        <div class="s-fit-quiz__result s-fit-quiz__result--{{ result.settings.band }} is-hidden" data-quiz-result="{{ result.settings.band }}" role="status" {{ result.shopify_attributes }}>
          {%- if result.settings.tag != blank -%}<span class="s-fit-quiz__result-tag">{{ result.settings.tag }}</span>{%- endif -%}
          {%- if result.settings.title != blank -%}<h3 class="s-fit-quiz__result-title">{{ result.settings.title }}</h3>{%- endif -%}
          {%- if result.settings.body != blank -%}<div class="s-fit-quiz__result-body">{{ result.settings.body }}</div>{%- endif -%}
          {%- if result.settings.expect != blank -%}
          <div class="s-fit-quiz__result-row"><span class="s-fit-quiz__result-row-label">{{ section.settings.expect_label }}</span><div class="s-fit-quiz__result-row-text">{{ result.settings.expect }}</div></div>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if result.settings.evidence != blank -%}
          <div class="s-fit-quiz__result-row"><span class="s-fit-quiz__result-row-label">{{ section.settings.evidence_label }}</span><div class="s-fit-quiz__result-row-text">{{ result.settings.evidence }}</div></div>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- comment -%} Filled by assets/main.js with the "note" of every answer the visitor picked (the questions people ask on TikTok: how to use it, minoxidil, timeline, proof). {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="s-fit-quiz__result-row s-fit-quiz__result-row--notes" data-quiz-notes hidden><span class="s-fit-quiz__result-row-label">{{ section.settings.notes_label }}</span><ul class="s-fit-quiz__notes"></ul></div>
          {%- if result.settings.show_cta and cta_label != blank -%}
          <a class="s-fit-quiz__cta custom-button" href="#{{ cta_target }}" data-scroll-to="{{ cta_target }}" data-quiz-tier="{{ tier }}">{{ cta_label }}</a>
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if section.settings.restart_label != blank -%}
          <button class="s-fit-quiz__restart" type="button" data-quiz-restart>{{ section.settings.restart_label }}</button>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>

    {%- if section.settings.footnote != blank -%}<p class="s-fit-quiz__footnote">{{ section.settings.footnote }}</p>{%- endif -%}
  </div>
</div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Hair-loss fit quiz",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "background",
      "label": "Tinted background",
      "default": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "default": "3 questions · 20 seconds"
    },
    {
      "type": "inline_richtext",
      "id": "title",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "Does pumpkin seed oil fit <em>your</em> hair loss?"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "text",
      "label": "Intro",
      "default": "<p>Women over 35 lose hair for a handful of reasons, and pumpkin seed oil works on one of them exceptionally well. Three quick questions and we’ll tell you honestly whether it’s yours - plus straight answers to the things people ask us most.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "step_label",
      "label": "Progress label",
      "default": "Question {current} of {total}",
      "info": "{current} and {total} are replaced with the numbers."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "back_label",
      "label": "Back button",
      "default": "← Back"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "restart_label",
      "label": "Start again link",
      "default": "Start again"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Result screens"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "expect_label",
      "label": "\"What to expect\" label",
      "default": "What to expect"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "evidence_label",
      "label": "\"What the research measured\" label",
      "default": "What the research measured"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "notes_label",
      "label": "\"Your question, answered\" label",
      "default": "Your question, answered",
      "info": "Heading of the box that repeats the answer notes of whatever the visitor picked."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "cta_label",
      "label": "Button label",
      "default": "See my bundle",
      "info": "Each result can override this."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "cta_link",
      "label": "Button link",
      "default": "#product-section",
      "info": "#product-section scrolls to the buy box and pre-selects the result's bundle tier."
    },
    {
      "type": "textarea",
      "id": "footnote",
      "label": "Footnote",
      "default": "The match is based on what pumpkin seed oil and caffeine were studied for (oral pumpkin seed oil, Cho et al. 2014; topical caffeine, Dhurat et al. 2017), not on a trial of Elaren’s finished formula. It is general information, not a diagnosis. Individual results vary."
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "question",
      "name": "Question",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "text",
          "label": "Question",
          "default": "What’s changed with your hair?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "hint",
          "label": "Hint (optional)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "option",
      "name": "Answer",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "range",
          "id": "question",
          "label": "Belongs to question",
          "min": 1,
          "max": 5,
          "step": 1,
          "default": 1,
          "info": "1 = the first Question block in the sidebar, 2 = the second, and so on."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "label",
          "label": "Answer",
          "default": "My part is wider and the crown looks thinner under the bathroom light"
        },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "band",
          "label": "Points to",
          "options": [
            {
              "value": "pattern",
              "label": "Hormonal pattern thinning (DHT)"
            },
            {
              "value": "shedding",
              "label": "Shedding after a trigger (telogen effluvium)"
            },
            {
              "value": "traction",
              "label": "Traction from tight styles"
            },
            {
              "value": "medical",
              "label": "See a doctor first"
            },
            {
              "value": "none",
              "label": "Nothing (neutral answer)"
            }
          ],
          "default": "pattern",
          "info": "A \"See a doctor first\" answer always decides the result, then \"Traction\", then whichever of pattern / shedding got more answers."
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "note",
          "label": "Answer shown on the result (optional)",
          "info": "Shown in the \"Your question, answered\" box of the result when this answer is picked. Use it for the things people ask before buying: how to use it, minoxidil, how long it takes."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "result",
      "name": "Result",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "band",
          "label": "Shown for",
          "options": [
            {
              "value": "pattern",
              "label": "Hormonal pattern thinning (DHT)"
            },
            {
              "value": "shedding",
              "label": "Shedding after a trigger (telogen effluvium)"
            },
            {
              "value": "traction",
              "label": "Traction from tight styles"
            },
            {
              "value": "medical",
              "label": "See a doctor first"
            }
          ],
          "default": "pattern"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "tag",
          "label": "Tag",
          "default": "Strong match"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "title",
          "label": "Title",
          "default": "Your thinning is the kind pumpkin seed oil was studied for"
        },
        {
          "type": "richtext",
          "id": "body",
          "label": "Text",
          "default": "<p>A part that keeps widening, a crown that shows more scalp each year, temples that creep back: that is hormonal pattern thinning, and after 35 it is the most common reason a woman loses hair. As oestrogen falls, follicles feel DHT more, and DHT shrinks each one a little more every cycle until the hair it grows is too fine to see.</p><p>Pumpkin seed oil’s plant sterols dampen the enzyme that makes DHT. That is the whole idea behind Elaren: cold-pressed pumpkin seed oil, massaged into the scalp where the thinning is, every night.</p>"
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "expect",
          "label": "What to expect",
          "default": "Two minutes on the scalp before bed, every night. Less hair in the brush within 2–4 weeks. Fine baby hairs along the part and hairline by month 2–3. Visible density over months 4–6, which is why the 3-month bundle is the one we recommend."
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "evidence",
          "label": "What the research measured",
          "default": "A 24-week randomised, placebo-controlled trial of pumpkin seed oil in pattern hair loss saw hair count rise 40%, four times the placebo group."
        },
        {
          "type": "checkbox",
          "id": "show_cta",
          "label": "Show the button",
          "default": true
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "cta_label",
          "label": "Button label override"
        },
        {
          "type": "range",
          "id": "bundle_tier",
          "label": "Pre-select bundle tier",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 5,
          "step": 1,
          "default": 2,
          "info": "The position of the tier in the Featured product section (1 = first card). 0 = leave the selection alone."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 30,
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Hair-loss fit quiz",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "text": "What’s changed with your hair?"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "option",
          "settings": {
            "question": 1,
            "label": "My part is wider and the crown looks thinner under the bathroom light",
            "band": "pattern"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "option",
          "settings": {
            "question": 1,
            "label": "My hairline or temples are creeping back",
            "band": "pattern"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "option",
          "settings": {
            "question": 1,
            "label": "My ponytail is half what it was and I lose handfuls in the shower",
            "band": "shedding"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "option",
          "settings": {
            "question": 1,
            "label": "Smooth bald patches, or a scalp that is sore, itchy or scarred",
            "band": "medical"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "text": "What do you think is behind it?"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "option",
          "settings": {
            "question": 2,
            "label": "It crept in over years, and thin hair runs in my family",
            "band": "pattern",
            "note": "Slow, inherited thinning is driven by DHT, a hormone that shrinks the follicle a little more every cycle. That is the exact step pumpkin seed oil’s plant sterols work on, and it is the reason Elaren is built around it."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "option",
          "settings": {
            "question": 2,
            "label": "It got worse with perimenopause or menopause",
            "band": "pattern",
            "note": "As oestrogen falls after 35, follicles feel DHT more. Pumpkin seed oil dampens the enzyme that makes DHT, which is why it is the active we lead with for women in this stage."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "option",
          "settings": {
            "question": 2,
            "label": "A baby, an illness, rapid weight loss or a brutal year",
            "band": "shedding",
            "note": "A shock to the body pushes a wave of follicles into rest at once and they let go two to three months later. It is common after weight-loss injections too. It usually recovers; the oil helps the hair that returns come back stronger."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "option",
          "settings": {
            "question": 2,
            "label": "Years of tight braids, buns, extensions or ponytails",
            "band": "traction",
            "note": "Pulling thins the edges and temples first. Nothing regrows while the tension stays, so the style has to change before the oil can help."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "text": "What do you most want a straight answer on?",
            "hint": "This one doesn’t change your result. It changes what we tell you."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "option",
          "settings": {
            "question": 3,
            "label": "How do I use it? Is it a pill, or does it go on my scalp?",
            "band": "none",
            "note": "It goes on your scalp, not in your mouth. Part your hair, squeeze a few drops onto the skin where it is thinning, massage for two minutes and leave it in overnight. Every night. One bottle is about 30 nights."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "option",
          "settings": {
            "question": 3,
            "label": "Can I use it with minoxidil, or instead of it?",
            "band": "none",
            "note": "Both. Elaren has no minoxidil and no hormones, so it does not compete with anything a doctor has prescribed. Using both: apply the minoxidil first, let it dry, then the oil. Many women use it on its own as the gentler option."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "option",
          "settings": {
            "question": 3,
            "label": "How long before I see anything, honestly?",
            "band": "none",
            "note": "Weeks 2–4: less hair in the brush and the drain. Months 2–3: fine baby hairs along the part and hairline. Months 4–6: visible density. Anyone promising faster is guessing. Do not stop at week three."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "option",
          "settings": {
            "question": 3,
            "label": "Is this real, or another oil that does nothing?",
            "band": "none",
            "note": "Fair question. Pumpkin seed oil has a 24-week placebo-controlled trial behind it, Elaren has 43 verified reviews you can read further down, and if your shedding has not eased after 30 nights we refund you. No photos, no awkward questions."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "result",
          "settings": {
            "band": "pattern",
            "tag": "Strong match",
            "title": "Your thinning is the kind pumpkin seed oil was studied for",
            "body": "<p>A part that keeps widening, a crown that shows more scalp each year, temples that creep back: that is hormonal pattern thinning, and after 35 it is the most common reason a woman loses hair. As oestrogen falls, follicles feel DHT more, and DHT shrinks each one a little more every cycle until the hair it grows is too fine to see.</p><p>Pumpkin seed oil’s plant sterols dampen the enzyme that makes DHT. That is the whole idea behind Elaren: cold-pressed pumpkin seed oil, massaged into the scalp where the thinning is, every night.</p>",
            "expect": "Two minutes on the scalp before bed, every night. Less hair in the brush within 2–4 weeks. Fine baby hairs along the part and hairline by month 2–3. Visible density over months 4–6, which is why the 3-month bundle is the one we recommend.",
            "evidence": "A 24-week randomised, placebo-controlled trial of pumpkin seed oil in pattern hair loss saw hair count rise 40%, four times the placebo group.",
            "show_cta": true,
            "bundle_tier": 2
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "result",
          "settings": {
            "band": "shedding",
            "tag": "Likely to help",
            "title": "This looks like shedding after a shock, and it usually recovers",
            "body": "<p>Hair that comes out all over a few months after a baby, an illness, surgery, rapid weight loss or a brutal year is telogen effluvium: a wave of follicles resting at once. The honest news is that most of it grows back on its own over 6–12 months.</p><p>Where pumpkin seed oil helps is the hair that returns: massaging it into the scalp nightly supports the follicle through regrowth and keeps DHT from quietly thinning what comes back, which matters more after 35.</p>",
            "expect": "The timeline is mostly your body’s. Shedding eases over the first weeks, new baby hairs along the hairline within 2–3 months. A 3-month bundle covers the recovery window.",
            "evidence": "Pumpkin seed oil was studied in pattern hair loss, not in shedding after a trigger. Here it supports regrowth; the recovery itself is your body’s.",
            "show_cta": true,
            "bundle_tier": 2
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "result",
          "settings": {
            "band": "traction",
            "tag": "Good match, with one condition",
            "title": "This is traction loss, and the style has to change first",
            "body": "<p>Thinning at the edges and temples that started with tight braids, extensions, buns or ponytails is traction alopecia. No oil regrows hair while the pulling continues. Loosen the style, give the edges a rest, and then pumpkin seed oil massaged into the scalp helps the recovery.</p>",
            "expect": "Once the tension is off, the fine hairs along the edges return over 2–4 months. If an area has been pulled tight for years and is smooth and shiny, see a dermatologist: that can be permanent.",
            "evidence": "Pumpkin seed oil was studied in pattern thinning, not in traction loss. Here it supports regrowth that only starts when the pulling stops.",
            "show_cta": true,
            "bundle_tier": 1
          }
        },
