          "type": "result",
          "settings": {
            "band": "medical",
            "tag": "See a doctor first",
            "title": "Please see a dermatologist before you buy anything",
            "body": "<p>Smooth round patches, or a scalp that is sore, inflamed or scarred, point to alopecia areata or a scarring alopecia. Those are medical conditions a topical oil does not address, and the earlier they are treated the better the outcome. We would rather you keep your money and get the right help.</p>",
            "expect": "Ask your GP for a referral to a dermatologist. If they rule those conditions out and find pattern thinning or shedding instead, come back: that is what pumpkin seed oil is for.",
            "evidence": "Pumpkin seed oil was studied in pattern hair loss. There is no evidence for it in autoimmune or scarring hair loss, so we do not claim any.",
            "show_cta": false,
            "bundle_tier": 0
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
